<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Entropy is defined as <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=\sum_{a}-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=\sum_{a}-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> and subject to the probability constraint <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. To compute its gradient subject to the constraint, we can make use of the method of Lagrange multipliers, where the gradient of <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> subject to <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> can be found by defining the Lagrangian <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(x,\lambda)=f(x)+\lambda g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(x,\lambda)=f(x)+\lambda g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\sum_{a}(-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))+\lambda\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}(-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\lambda\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}((\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\sum_{a}(-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))+\lambda\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}(-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\lambda\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}((\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we can compute its gradient with the product rule:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\left[-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right]-\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}1\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\lambda,\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\left[-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right]-\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}1\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\lambda,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where the last term is null. Given that <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log\pi(a|s)=\frac{\nabla\pi(a|s)}{\pi(a|s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\pi(a|s)=\frac{\nabla\pi(a|s)}{\pi(a|s)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can replace <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> in the second term, obtaining:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\frac{\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)}{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)}\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+1-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\frac{\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)}{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)}\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\\
&amp;=-\sum_{a}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+1-\lambda)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Since the aim is to maximize entropy, we need to find where all partial derivatives are equal to 0, i.e., where the original constraint <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1=0</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied, and when <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+1-\lambda=0,\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+1-\lambda=0,\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. The last set of equations shows that all <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> must be equal; under the constraint, this means that <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|},\forall a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|},\forall a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1+\log\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}=1+\log 1-\log|\mathcal{A}|=1-\log|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1+\log\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}=1+\log 1-\log|\mathcal{A}|=1-\log|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&lt;\lambda-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&lt;\lambda-1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&lt;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&lt;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sign of the gradient is positive, and the probability gets increased; vice versa, when <math id="A1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&gt;\lambda-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&gt;\lambda-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the sign of the gradient becomes negative, and the probability is decreased.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Disequilibrium is defined as <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and subject to the probability constraint <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, we can make use of the method of the Lagrange multipliers, obtaining:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\right)^{2}+\lambda\left(\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-1\right)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}^{2}(a|s)+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|^{2}}-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)+\lambda\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}^{2}(a|s)-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\lambda\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\lambda\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}^{2}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\lambda.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\right)^{2}+\lambda\left(\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-1\right)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}^{2}(a|s)+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|^{2}}-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)+\lambda\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\lambda\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}^{2}(a|s)-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\lambda\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\lambda\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}^{2}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\lambda.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Its gradient with respect to <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(2\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(2\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\right)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\theta},\lambda)&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(2\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\right)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left(2\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}\right)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">In order to find the optimum, we need to set all partial derivatives equal to 0, including with respect to <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., that the original constraint <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=\sum_{a}(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s))-1=0</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied, plus that <math id="A1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}=0,\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|-2}{|\mathcal{A}|}=0,\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. These equations are true for <math id="A1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. But since we also have the original constraint, <math id="A1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\frac{\lambda}{2}-1=1-\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|}{2}-1=-\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}-\frac{\lambda}{2}-1=1-\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|}{2}-1=-\frac{\lambda|\mathcal{A}|}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> must be equal to zero; thus, <math id="A1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|},\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|},\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. As expected, the minimum lies where the distribution is equiprobable. When <math id="A1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&lt;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&lt;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient is negative, causing the probability of selecting action <math id="A1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> to decrease further. Conversely, when <math id="A1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&gt;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)&gt;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient becomes positive, leading to an increase in the probability of selecting action <math id="A1.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, complexity is defined as <math id="A1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)</annotation></semantics></math>. According to the product rule, its gradient is as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}&amp;C[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)+D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left[2S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\right)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\left(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+1\right)\right]\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left[2S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\right]\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}&amp;C[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)=S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)+D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left[2S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\left(\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\right)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\left(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)+1\right)\right]\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)\\
&amp;=\sum_{a}\left[2S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\right]\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">However, as for entropy and disequilibrium, complexity is subject to the probability constraint <math id="A1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math> as well. To find the local optima of complexity, we need to find where the partial derivatives of the Lagrangian <math id="A1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-\lambda(\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-\lambda(\sum_{a}\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-1)</annotation></semantics></math> are equal to 0, i.e., to solve the equation system composed of the probability constraint plus <math id="A1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-\lambda=0,\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)-\frac{2}{|\mathcal{A}|}S[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-D[\pi_{\bm{\theta}}](s)-\lambda=0,\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. This system has multiple solutions, i.e., where <math id="A1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|},\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a|s)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|},\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (which represents the local minimum and complexity is equal to 0), plus <math id="A1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math> maxima that are the recombination of the same set of probabilities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The experiments were carried out on a system equipped with a 32-core AMD EPYC 7413 processor and an NVIDIA L40 GPU, running Python version 3.10.18. We used the <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch</span> library and leveraged the <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stable-baselines3</span> implementation of PPO, which was modified into CDPO according to Algorithm <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Complexity-Driven Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="165.65" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 165.65" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,165.65) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#333333;" fill="#333333" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 160.33 C 0 163.27 2.38 165.65 5.32 165.65 L 544.68 165.65 C 547.62 165.65 550 163.27 550 160.33 L 550 5.32 C 550 2.38 547.62 0 544.68 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 145.05 L 548.62 145.05 L 548.62 5.32 C 548.62 3.15 546.85 1.38 544.68 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 6.92 151.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="523.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.81em;">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Python implementation of CDPO complexity loss</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 6.92 12.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.81em;--ltx-fo-height:8.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="122.38" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 122.38)" width="523.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.81em;">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\cdot\cdot\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot\cdot\cdot</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathtt{dist=self.policy.get\_distribution(rollout\_data.observations)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚝</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚜𝚎𝚕𝚏</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚙𝚘𝚕𝚒𝚌𝚢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚐𝚎𝚝</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">_</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚒𝚋𝚞𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚛𝚘𝚕𝚕𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">_</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚊𝚝𝚊</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚘𝚋𝚜𝚎𝚛𝚟𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚜</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{dist=self.policy.get\_distribution(rollout\_data.observations)}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{probs=dist.distribution.probs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚋𝚜</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚝</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚒𝚋𝚞𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚋𝚜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{probs=dist.distribution.probs}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{entropy=dist.distribution.entropy()}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚛𝚘𝚙𝚢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚝</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚒𝚋𝚞𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚛𝚘𝚙𝚢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{entropy=dist.distribution.entropy()}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathtt{disequilibrium=torch.sum((probs-1.0/probs.size(-1))^{**}2,dim=-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚎𝚚𝚞𝚒𝚕𝚒𝚋𝚛𝚒𝚞𝚖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚝𝚘𝚛𝚌𝚑</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚜𝚞𝚖</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚋𝚜</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="monospace">1.0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚋𝚜</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚜𝚒𝚣𝚎</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟷</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟸</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟷</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{disequilibrium=torch.sum((probs-1.0/probs.size(-1))^{**}2,dim=-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{complexity=entropy*disequilibrium}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚌𝚘𝚖𝚙𝚕𝚎𝚡𝚒𝚝𝚢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚛𝚘𝚙𝚢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚎𝚚𝚞𝚒𝚕𝚒𝚋𝚛𝚒𝚞𝚖</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{complexity=entropy*disequilibrium}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{complexity\_loss=-torch.mean(complexity)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚌𝚘𝚖𝚙𝚕𝚎𝚡𝚒𝚝𝚢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚕𝚘𝚜𝚜</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚝𝚘𝚛𝚌𝚑</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚖𝚎𝚊𝚗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚌𝚘𝚖𝚙𝚕𝚎𝚡𝚒𝚝𝚢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{complexity\_loss=-torch.mean(complexity)}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A2.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\cdot\cdot\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot\cdot\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The adopted neural networks followed the default architectures provided by <span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stable-baselines3</span>. For 1D observation space environments, i.e., CartPole and CARTerpillar environments, we used an MLP with 2 fully connected layers with 64 units each. For image observation spaces, i.e., CarRacing and Atari environments, we used a Nature CNN architecture for feature extraction, with a sequence of 2D convolutional layers with layer sizes <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[32,64,64]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[32,64,64]</annotation></semantics></math>, kernel sizes <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[(8,8),(4,4),(3,3)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[(8,8),(4,4),(3,3)]</annotation></semantics></math>, and strides <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[(4,4),(2,2),(1,1)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[(4,4),(2,2),(1,1)]</annotation></semantics></math>, with ReLU activation function. The output is then flattened and passed through a dense layer (of dimension 256 for CarRacing and 512 for Atari games) with ReLU activation.
Finally, consistent with the original CoinRun experiments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, we used the IMPALA CNN architecture <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Espeholt et al., 2018</a>)</cite> with three layers, each consisting of a 2D convolutional layer, a 2D max-pooling operation with kernel size 3 and stride 2, followed by two residual blocks. Each residual block contains two 2D convolutional layers preceded by ReLU activation functions, and their output is summed with their input. All the convolutional layers inside the three IMPALA layers have the same size (<math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[16,32,32]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[16,32,32]</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively), and the same stride of 3. Finally, the output is flattened and passed through a dense layer of dimension 256 with ReLU activation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The full list of training hyperparameters is reported in Table <a href="#A2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Complexity-Driven Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
